#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "361ff4ea-4bf0-5084-ae3e-e6b810cba5cd" :knowledge-point/title "Optimizing the Area of a Rectangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15350554-e886-5e11-8207-77bbb3e0bec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.93\\,{m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399421} {:answer/id #uuid "fb654c8f-375d-5fa0-b333-4fd2c3d1805a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.72\\,{m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399422} {:answer/id #uuid "2b6c956a-c96c-5420-a899-8859c8a907f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.35\\,{m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399423} {:answer/id #uuid "3a202375-39cd-502a-81cb-6cca990bb170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.06\\,{m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399424} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bc53a0-6be4-5825-a047-05acf7782f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.08\\,{m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a202375-39cd-502a-81cb-6cca990bb170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.06\\,{m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399424} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9367409-a53f-579f-8cdb-a83c5faaa2a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1af9295c-5eff-510e-ba44-71a6e28cc19c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104195" :question/problem "A gardener wants to fence a rectangular flowerbed with $15$ meters of fencing. To two decimal places, what is the largest area that he can make with the fencing?" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: Let us call $x$ and $y$ the dimensions of the rectangle.\n\n![](images/be/bebb7c4ca5e38d75136146f6e4547b0e72d529ce24453a3d0212bca1ffbfe4c0.png)\n\n**Step 2**: We need to find the values of $x$ and $y$ such as the area\n\n$$\nA=xy\n$$\n\nis the greatest possible value.\n\n**Step 3**: This is subject to the constraint that the perimeter is $15.$ This gives the equation\n\n$$\n2x+2y=15.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We make one of the variables the subject in the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =15 \\\\ y & =\\frac{15}{2}-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=\\frac{15}{2}-x$ in the expression $A=xy$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =x(\\frac{15}{2}-x) \\\\ A & =\\frac{15}{2}x-{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We solve the equation ${A}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(x)=\\frac{15}{2}-2x,\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{15}{2}-2x & =0 \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 6**: We confirm that $x=\\frac{15}{4}$ is a maximum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{A}^{″}(x)=-2\\,⟹\\,{A}^{″}(\\frac{15}{4})=-2<0.\n$$\n\nSince ${A}^{″}(\\frac{15}{4})$ is negative, we conclude that $x=\\frac{15}{4}$ is indeed a maximum of $A(x).$\n\nFinally, when $x=\\frac{15}{4}$, we have \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{15}{2}-\\frac{15}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the dimensions of the rectangle with the largest area are $x=\\frac{15}{4}$ and $y=\\frac{15}{4},$ and we conclude that\n\n$$\nA=xy=\\frac{15}{4}\\cdot \\frac{15}{4}≈14.06\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc967c7-840e-5717-98f2-330fcf0fe12d" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Definition of Left- and Right-Continuity to Compute a Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "876c0dae-0a07-5814-87cc-25b89309bb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239231} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf3e2a2-4247-5797-907c-b9cd274cdc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239702} {:answer/id #uuid "be1327a4-7929-5e44-b25b-4b05f4f9face" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239713} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd24695-98ee-581e-92ce-34ab9ccb7fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239991} {:answer/id #uuid "eafd65b4-ea1a-5e69-a7cc-1632c2d74394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eafd65b4-ea1a-5e69-a7cc-1632c2d74394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240121} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1122c81-059d-5890-845b-a7dc9687558c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f74b17a-b71c-5fd1-b977-bfbf3cab75b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104283" :question/problem "If $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-5$ and ${lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}f(x)=3,$ then what is ${lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}(f(x)-2f(-5))?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-5,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}f(x)=f(-5)=3.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}(f(x)-2f(-5)) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}f(x)-2f(-5) \\\\  & =3-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096617 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b194bf2f-feaa-5656-a3ee-0ff466a39e77" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20897b11-31f3-5236-8344-066364ab30aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238339} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9dc0f2-2211-5b4e-a2e7-26a81ec7f21c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x+sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238465} {:answer/id #uuid "528c811e-a747-5b55-b5c7-a2d707220097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238765} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cd3281-ae65-5560-8442-2a603e50ff12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}cos⁡x+sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239827} {:answer/id #uuid "cce47b31-03c3-57e4-ae08-02ac34ba2a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x+{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "528c811e-a747-5b55-b5c7-a2d707220097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238765} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0d6216-93d3-5d7b-aefb-cbdf2e8a0a46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d7240cf-a773-5ae8-8c7e-03955317789e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104297" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}cos⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}cos⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (cos⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(cos⁡x)+({e}^{x})(-sin⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7ad9a7-4c9d-545c-82eb-9c76932cadd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{5})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{5})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238886} {:answer/id #uuid "6a078f3f-2a60-5526-a8ba-3f16e6cfb1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238974} {:answer/id #uuid "8859da1a-7852-51d3-b95c-34c514573554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239241} {:answer/id #uuid "ab48ba5c-ec26-5b84-bae6-309aaaa6e43d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239551} {:answer/id #uuid "c6aed593-ea59-59c9-8d77-811d9a8d1ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a078f3f-2a60-5526-a8ba-3f16e6cfb1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238974} :answer-field/id #uuid "60880ad2-84d2-5b41-86ef-530634bc2f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eba0abc0-d36a-5439-b495-fad6bb86a003" :question/math-academy-id "q-104343" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{6}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}}=[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{-5}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =3\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}} & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{-5} \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(-5)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(-5)\\theta )] \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )]=6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd281121-21d3-5dc4-8537-af248d0fdf46" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Vector Field Corresponding to a Given Potential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45db7d37-257e-5741-9767-a2ee72bc303f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+2y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238662} {:answer/id #uuid "a026c4f1-65e8-584a-81f8-49d09aed3845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239453} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b3803d-0406-5f4c-b4f7-02086d600d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239500} {:answer/id #uuid "b49e4fa1-e304-508a-b582-63a15e87c038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239636} {:answer/id #uuid "c17f4964-aa3f-54ce-b990-6a3cc4bcb36c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{2y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6b3803d-0406-5f4c-b4f7-02086d600d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239500} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dcac30f-063e-5f3e-b8eb-a855b3db8035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "139d3292-e475-5138-868b-b4cb7235237f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104397" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1})j \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd281121-21d3-5dc4-8537-af248d0fdf46" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Vector Field Corresponding to a Given Potential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7109fa2b-c389-5fc6-b0c4-b41d4d74bf4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\,i-y\\,j-4z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382691} {:answer/id #uuid "e9db5c91-f335-58aa-97c3-99952996d70f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i-2y\\,j-2z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382692} {:answer/id #uuid "0631570a-280c-5f08-a196-767cab352a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\,i-2y\\,j-4z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382693} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7f9857-e151-5110-9b90-a5c8c453d023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\,i+2y\\,j+4z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382694} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc25693-095f-5e5b-8994-90d409ec8817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x\\,i-y\\,j-2z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0631570a-280c-5f08-a196-767cab352a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\,i-2y\\,j-4z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382693} :answer-field/id #uuid "777faee0-1b4e-5ed3-9d6b-efa0173e6d16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99ded14c-42f7-5e12-a882-b682276e471b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104402" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =6x\\,i-2y\\,j-4z\\,k \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=6x\\,i-2y\\,j-4z\\,k.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8d73fd7-cdeb-59f1-a84c-aab6defb3aa3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Parameter in a Given Conservative Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad87b50-24eb-5866-a7a3-616f4089f740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163379} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d86d76-1ed0-5562-a0b6-7e81a5bdd6a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163380} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8a7e19-8534-5440-a04f-59429a4c1084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163381} {:answer/id #uuid "1bcf0893-e2c6-53b9-ac36-110666bdc913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163382} {:answer/id #uuid "62273ef4-b30a-5ac7-bfb0-b7ed3c358094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163383}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2cd8df0e-a91d-558b-bb05-ba85ed8ba7d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5cc30dd-c54c-510e-a8ae-905a8e5f5570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382711} {:answer/id #uuid "c34ca81d-7ee1-541d-b3dd-2ca1a9a7b794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382712} {:answer/id #uuid "ed208e02-eb59-5dac-832b-a002914d41da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382713} {:answer/id #uuid "6f96d04c-ea2f-566b-890a-1654a4e46ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382714} {:answer/id #uuid "6b74b360-5da5-5315-8da6-0afc30df25d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f96d04c-ea2f-566b-890a-1654a4e46ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382714} :answer-field/id #uuid "09bd8799-4e53-54b3-b672-a9390042cbde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2658d9bc-59d5-580d-bbeb-6f2b334d98b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-104412" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=(x-a){e}^{x+y}\\,i+x{e}^{x+y}\\,j$ on ${R}^{2}$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ the domain $D={R}^{2},$ and we have \n\n$$\nP=(x-a){e}^{x+y},\\,Q=x{e}^{x+y}.\n$$\n\n \nComputing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=(x-a){e}^{x+y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=(x+1){e}^{x+y}.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a){e}^{x+y} & =(x+1){e}^{x+y} \\\\ (x-a){e}^{x+y}-(x+1){e}^{x+y} & =0 \\\\ (x-a-x-1){e}^{x+y} & =0 \\\\ -(a+1){e}^{x+y} & =0 \\\\ a & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cofactor Method To Solve for an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3907885c-b8d9-5a8a-b101-b8bacd3c100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238548} {:answer/id #uuid "59dc3dbc-a563-5ed7-a2b8-0b53ab3690df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238829} {:answer/id #uuid "7219f929-3c4c-5130-ba67-06b6ec68f6bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239034} {:answer/id #uuid "e1294134-a47b-51be-972a-dbe70aba54ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240033} {:answer/id #uuid "e666f6f4-3b9a-508e-addb-22f8d57a69de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3907885c-b8d9-5a8a-b101-b8bacd3c100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238548} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d4629b7-d427-5661-a6f1-3af0b7b88fc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55417378-dec5-552f-8b04-ebd15181a9f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104439" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=k-4.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-4\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{22}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{k-4} \\\\ k-4 & =-4 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e705d0a-4f00-58c5-bfa3-0640c06a24cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238461} {:answer/id #uuid "950e015a-4dbb-56c7-9552-5f98ebc267f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239344} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d5826c-0581-5379-9a42-fe9bbf00aba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239915} {:answer/id #uuid "eceb79d2-6cd4-5cc9-bccd-243524ee9bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240138} {:answer/id #uuid "eeae5780-1ac7-5634-88fc-1ad4eb87c4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eceb79d2-6cd4-5cc9-bccd-243524ee9bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240138} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d5a9ca-fa2d-5f5e-8810-22ea172d70d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1d55ff1-19e4-58c5-a23a-1cef5eceb55b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104453" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-6$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-6$ | $-2\\pi $ | $3\\pi $ | $5$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+2g(x))$ at $x=-6.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+2g(x))={f}^{′}(x)+2{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-6$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)+2g(x))|}_{x=-6} & ={f}^{′}(-6)+2{g}^{′}(-6) \\\\  & =5+2(-2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180ef558-9ed6-5cce-9dca-f397cbca2a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238260} {:answer/id #uuid "6abfd956-c66a-5d7e-9340-3d2575686da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238980} {:answer/id #uuid "80bf18c2-7c82-59a1-b1d0-128cc04043f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239173} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5e41f2-4fd2-5db5-81f2-fd469f282128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239553} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a37964-a889-594f-a3c0-5f08cd37e2c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6abfd956-c66a-5d7e-9340-3d2575686da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238980} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2da357a-9c04-5bb4-a19d-1edcb5991e71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b7607d8-f365-578e-840c-7619cca90194" :question/math-academy-id "q-104469" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59074ef9-086c-58ad-a7d8-980d9b9a9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+27x-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238822} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca38533-c4df-51e5-9004-4d767f6b1121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239132} {:answer/id #uuid "8ecac77e-8d0d-508c-ac20-d5475ce11dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+18x+45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239297} {:answer/id #uuid "c38ecfd2-1368-5e2e-bdfa-5d7b64a17003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-9x+70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239782} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e60595-83e9-5b02-941d-642dfd9e5c6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}-27x-135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ca38533-c4df-51e5-9004-4d767f6b1121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239132} :answer-field/id #uuid "81c9fddb-f906-537a-9707-e0d41a21b3d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a483d6da-3355-5ef5-a0a8-57b7cc6e7d69" :question/math-academy-id "q-104487" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-5))(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+5)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+5)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3(x+5)({x}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3(x+5)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{3}+9x+5{x}^{2}+45) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cf627a0-6921-58ee-91c0-2f225d425711" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Transpose of a Row Vector or Column Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "833663bf-3970-5af6-8e3a-39f84ce0af74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056156} {:answer/id #uuid "848e9a7a-7c07-5311-acc3-3f32cc5e5be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056157} {:answer/id #uuid "88494fb1-c066-508f-b55b-d80ff6428bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 4 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056158} {:answer/id #uuid "ce89aba2-05bf-5b03-9f7b-8c7a1ac5d7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\